    ],
    "summary": "I built a single-column tower three storeys tall from three north-half hex bases stacked at cell (0,0). It has a drawer on the bottom storey and an open bin with two compartments on the top storey. I used half bases because drawers only go on the cut face of a half base, and the configurator only lets a base sit on top of the same kind, so all three storeys are halves. I ran the house rules: end caps on the open faces (7 caps, including the middle storey's cut face) and the joint bolting. No cover goes on top, so the bin stays open. check_build passes with no issues and the mesh collision check reads clear. The build has 25 parts, about 1446 g of filament and about 2053 minutes of printing. I didn't add any props because the brief didn't describe a use.",
    "outcome": "built"
  },
