          "name": "finish",
          "arguments": "{\"outcome\":\"built\",\"summary\":\"I built a single-column tower three storeys tall from three north-half hex bases stacked at cell (0,0). It has a drawer on the bottom storey and an open bin with two compartments on the top storey. I used half bases because drawers only go on the cut face of a half base, and the configurator only lets a base sit on top of the same kind, so all three storeys are halves. I ran the house rules: end caps on the open faces (7 caps, including the middle storey's cut face) and the joint bolting. No cover goes on top, so the bin stays open. check_build passes with no issues and the mesh collision check reads clear. The build has 25 parts, about 1446 g of filament and about 2053 minutes of printing. I didn't add any props because the brief didn't describe a use.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"Three storeys tall\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Bases piece:0,0,0, piece:0,0,1 and piece:0,0,2 (all north halves) are stacked and joined by snaps.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Drawers on the bottom storey\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"drawer:0#0,0#cut is on the cut face of the bottom base. It's a single drawer because a one-column tower has only one cut face on that storey.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Open bins on the top storey\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"bin:0,0,2~hex-bin-half-n-full-div2 is a full-depth bin with two compartments and nothing covering its top.\"}]}"
